# backslash-active-comment: Does a backslash at the end of an active comment line swallow the next line (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: v@3=2
# pc: ODE0038,ODE0076
# ruling: the active comment line swallows the next line as a `#` comment does; `x'=1` is lost and `x'=2` stays. PhaseCont keeps the active comment as raw text with the unsupported warning and gives ODE0076 for the swallowed line (language.md, Lines).
"an active comment \
x'=1
x'=2
x(0)=0
aux v=x
@ total=1,dt=0.5,meth=euler
